82. MEDIA SECURITY

Never place private provider credentials inside:

- React source
- ".env" variables beginning with "VITE_"
- APK assets
- JavaScript bundles
- localStorage
- public configuration files

Any secret API key must remain server-side.

The client should receive only the data it actually needs.

IMPORTANT:

The previously exposed ZST API key must NOT be committed into the repository.

If a secret has already been exposed, treat it as compromised and recommend rotation rather than reusing it.

