87. NETWORK TIMEOUTS

Every network request must have sensible timeout and cancellation behavior.

Avoid requests hanging forever.

When a request fails:

- stop loading
- show appropriate UI
- provide retry
- clean up pending state

Abort obsolete search requests when a new query replaces them.

---

88. SEARCH PERFORMANCE

Search should not fire a network request for every individual keystroke without control.

Use debouncing where appropriate.

Cancel obsolete requests.

Avoid race conditions where an older response overwrites a newer search.

